{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST expose a `list_files` tool with this interface:\n\n```text\nlist_files({ path: String = \".\" }) -> Array<DirectoryEntry>\n\nDirectoryEntry {\n    path: String,\n    kind: \"file\" | \"directory\",\n}\n```\n\nThe tool MUST list the immediate children of the requested directory, returning\nproject-relative paths. Each listed directory MUST contain a visible file.\nA failed listing MUST return an explanatory tool error. Directory listings\nMUST NOT become evidence inputs.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged this from the supplied test sources only, because they exercise every obligation in `requirements.authoring.file_discovery`. I did not request implementation source.\n\n**Interface and default path.**\n- `additional_read_flow_searches_outlines_and_reads_a_rust_file` calls `list_files` with `{}`. It checks that `src` comes back as `kind: \"directory\"`. It then lists that directory and asserts the exact result `[{\"path\":\"src/lib.rs\",\"kind\":\"file\"}]`.\n- `reading_records_only_delivered_sources_and_their_terms` and `source_tools_share_sdk_visibility_for_untracked_files` pass an explicit `path` and assert exact entries with `path` and `kind`.\n\n**Immediate children, project-relative paths.**\n- The exact-equality assertions above check that only the immediate children appear, with project-relative paths such as `src/lib.rs` and `src/draft.rs`.\n- `listed_git_directories_need_an_eligible_descendant_at_any_depth` lists `a` and asserts exactly `[{\"path\":\"a/b\",\"kind\":\"directory\"}]`.\n- `large_listings_and_outlines_page_whole_entries_in_order` checks that 800 entries come back whole, in sorted order, each once, across pages.\n\n**Each listed directory contains a visible file.**\n- `listed_git_directories_need_an_eligible_descendant_at_any_depth` asserts that `a` is listed. It contains only `b`, which holds an eligible file two levels down, so this covers a descendant at any depth.\n- The same test asserts that `blocked-only` is absent. Its only file is git-ignored.\n- `source_tools_share_sdk_visibility_for_untracked_files` asserts that the ignored `src/build` directory is not listed. The same test also covers files hidden by ignore rules.\n- `outside_symlinks_are_excluded_from_reads_search_and_discovery` asserts that symlinks to outside directories and files are not listed, and that listing `outside` fails.\n\n**Failed listing returns an explanatory tool error.**\n- `failed_listings_return_explanatory_tool_errors` covers a missing path, a file given as the path, a non-string path, and an unknown extra field. Each asserts an error message containing a relevant word (`cannot`, `cannot list`, `path`, `extra`). It also asserts the error kind is not `PermissionDenied`, so these are recoverable tool errors.\n- `unpermitted_requests_outside_the_project_are_recoverable_tool_errors` asserts that a listing outside the project errors with a message containing \"outside\".\n- `search_merges_context_windows_and_respects_ignore_rules` asserts that `../` fails.\n- `outside_symlinks_are_excluded_from_reads_search_and_discovery` asserts that listing a path that resolves outside the project fails.\n\n**Listings are not evidence inputs.**\n- Several tests assert `inputs.is_empty()` on `list_files` results: `listed_git_directories_need_an_eligible_descendant_at_any_depth`, `additional_read_flow_searches_outlines_and_reads_a_rust_file`, and `reading_records_only_delivered_sources_and_their_terms`.\n- `large_listings_and_outlines_page_whole_entries_in_order` asserts the same for each paged result.\n\nAn empty directory with no files at all is not tested separately. It falls in the same class as `blocked-only`, a directory with no visible file. The text makes no further distinction, so I do not count it as a gap.\n\nAll of these tests carry `{test}` references to the requirement, so there is no marking gap. I found no obligation without a test and no assertion that contradicts the text.",
  "references": "189d4f12694fb02013f38458393f585ca2629adf8e7b395fce8a30254185ef2b",
